# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit real values.
#
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the client bundle and is public by
# definition. Server-side secrets belong in Supabase Edge Function secrets
# (`supabase secrets set NAME=value`), not here.

# ── Supabase (public) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# ── Stripe (publishable key only — never the secret key) ──────────────────────
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_your-key

# ── Analytics (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID=
VITE_ADSENSE_ID=

# ── AWS Lambda endpoints (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_AWS_LAMBDA_CHAT_COMPLETION_URL=
VITE_AWS_LAMBDA_IMAGE_EDIT_URL=
VITE_AWS_LAMBDA_IMAGE_GENERATION_URL=

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The values below are NOT read by the frontend. They are listed so the required
# set is documented in one place; set them as Edge Function secrets:
#
#   supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=... TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=...
#
#   RESEND_API_KEY          transactional email
#   EMAIL_FROM              verified sender address
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID      SMS
#   TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN
#   TWILIO_PHONE_NUMBER
#   PORTAL_URL              canonical portal origin for signing links
#   ESIGN_ALLOWED_PORTALS   extra approved portal origins, comma-separated
#   CRON_SECRET             shared secret for the scheduled workers
#
# ── ALLOWED_ORIGINS — SET THIS BEFORE THE NEXT FUNCTION DEPLOY ────────────────
# The browser origins allowed to call the Edge Functions, comma-separated. Every
# function used to answer Access-Control-Allow-Origin: '*'; they now answer with
# the caller's origin only when it appears here (PORTAL_URL and
# ESIGN_ALLOWED_PORTALS are folded in automatically, so an origin already listed
# there does not need repeating).
#
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.yourco.com,https://*.vercel.app
#
# An entry may be an exact origin or carry ONE wildcard label for preview
# deployments ("https://*.vercel.app"). The wildcard matches a single label and
# never crosses a dot.
#
# IF THIS IS UNSET IN PRODUCTION, browser calls from the app are refused with
# 403 and the portal stops working — the failure is loud and immediate rather
# than silent, which is the point, but it means this must be set in the same
# change that deploys the functions. Non-browser callers are unaffected: the
# M-Pesa callback, dealer servers using x-api-key and the schedulers send no
# Origin header at all, and CORS does not apply to them.
#
# With NO allowlist configured, only localhost is accepted — enough for
# `supabase functions serve`, never enough for a deployment.
#
# ── Encryption keys ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These two open data that is stored ONLY as ciphertext. They are not
# credentials that can be reissued: lose one and the data it protects is
# unrecoverable, because the database never holds the key. Back them up
# somewhere outside Supabase before going live, and never commit them.
#
#   MPESA_CRED_ENC_KEY      tenant Daraja credentials (mpesa_tenant_credentials)
#   PII_ENC_KEY             employee bank account / NSSF / next-of-kin ID
#                           (employee_private_data, via the employee-pii function)
#
# Any passphrase length works — each is hashed to a 32-byte AES-256-GCM key.
# Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 48
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
